g if needed, and it centralizes the queen effectively.\n\nReason:  \n**Q: d8-d5** wins a knight immediately as it's undefended, and White has no piece that can defend it in one move. After Qd5, the knight on e5 is attacked and cannot escape easily — the only flight square (c4 or d3) would require two moves. This gives Black a clear material advantage early in the game.\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-d5"}
